<title>USA: TABLE - Carpenter Technology Q4 net rises.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Carpenter Technology Q4 net rises.</headline>
<dateline>READING, Pa. 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>(In Thousands, Except Per Share Data)</p>
<p>			     Three Months Ended	 Year Ended</p>
<p>				    June 30		   June 30</p>
<p>				  1997     1996	   1997     1996</p>
<p> NET SALES		$284,715 $237,455     $939,000 $865,324</p>
<p>COSTS AND EXPENSES:</p>
<p>   Cost of sales	 208,552  168,774	697,892  636,783</p>
<p>Selling and</p>
<p>administrative</p>
<p>    expenses		36,160   31,218	126,357  112,893</p>
<p>   Interest expense	5,803    4,522	 19,930   18,935</p>
<p>Equity in loss of</p>
<p>    joint venture	    266	705	  1,188    7,025</p>
<p>   Other income, net   (3,483)  (1,872)	(4,238)  (5,482)</p>
<p>			     247,298  203,347	841,129  770,154</p>
<p>INCOME BEFORE</p>
<p>  INCOME TAXES	    37,417   34,108	 97,871   95,170</p>
<p> Income taxes	     14,640   12,885	 37,878   35,022</p>
<p> NET INCOME		 22,777   21,223	 59,993   60,148</p>
<p>EARNINGS PER COMMON SHARE:</p>
<p>   Primary		    1.14     1.24	   3.30     3.51</p>
<p>   Fully diluted	    1.10     1.19	   3.16     3.38</p>
<p>Weighted average common</p>
<p>  shares outstanding    19,609   16,734	 17,703   16,677</p>
<p>NOTE: The company said higher revenues for Q4 and year-end 1997 resulted from contributions of Dynamet Inc, acquired in February 1997.</p>
<p>The company said net income improved in Q4 as a result of the Dynamet acquisition and increased sales of ceramic products.</p>
<p>Carpenter Technology Corp.</p>
</text>
